    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0239" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1494</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-26T15:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1915, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Hukuang bridge specifications, prepared by Cox, require shop erection. Managing
                    director refuses to modify, considering requirement proper. I beg to request
                    instructions as to how far to press protest and whether American manufacturers
                    are willing to guarantee fit of bridges without shop erection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
